    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fe432661-5baa-5b98-badd-2753010278bb",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "If $\\cos x=-\\frac{10}{11},$ then $\\cos (x-16\\pi )=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=\\cos x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos x=\\cos (x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-8$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\cos x &=\\cos (x+2\\cdot (-8)\\cdot \\pi )=\\cos (x-16\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos x=-\\frac{10}{11},$ then $\\cos (x-16\\pi )=-\\frac{10}{11}.$",
